        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(imessage): remove split-send coalescing config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #91243.\n\nOpenClaw still carried an iMessage-side `channels.imessage.coalesceSameSenderDms` option and monitor debounce/merge path that existed only to compensate for Apple URL-preview split-sends before `imsg` handled them upstream. With `imsg >= 0.11.1` now the supported floor for this cleanup, that fallback adds latency and config surface without owning the canonical behavior anymore.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Removes the OpenClaw iMessage split-send coalescing config from the typed config, zod schema, generated channel metadata, docs, and tests.\n- Removes the monitor-specific debounce override, DM coalescing branch, URL-balloon merge gate, and stale helper exports.\n- Adds `openclaw doctor --fix` cleanup for stale top-level and per-account `coalesceSameSenderDms` keys.\n- Keeps normal runtime/config validation strict: stale `coalesceSameSenderDms` is repaired only in the doctor migration path, not silently stripped during runtime validation.\n- Enforces the `imsg >= 0.11.1` floor in the iMessage probe/startup path and documents it in setup guidance.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers on current `imsg` get immediate iMessage DM dispatch without the old OpenClaw split-send debounce. Existing configs that still contain `channels.imessage.coalesceSameSenderDms` are rejected by strict runtime validation until `openclaw doctor --fix` removes the stale key from disk. Users with older `imsg` binaries now get a clear fatal probe error telling them to upgrade before enabling iMessage.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `7bf57b48914b56df6d45887bca31ee7454fae716`.\n\n- ClawSweeper P2 fixed: `src/config/validation.ts` no longer strips `channels.imessage.coalesceSameSenderDms`; `src/config/config.legacy-config-detection.accepts-imessage-dmpolicy.test.ts` proves normal raw validation preserves the stale key so doctor owns cleanup.\n- Doctor repair proof, local isolated temp install: `OPENCLAW_HOME`, `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, and `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH` pointed at a temp config containing both top-level and per-account `coalesceSameSenderDms`; `pnpm dev doctor --fix --yes` exited 0, printed both removal lines, completed doctor, and the post-run JSON check reported `hasTop=false`, `hasAccount=false`.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox proof on `blacksmith-testbox` lease `tbx_01kxh12fc9rnmyg73374rkvp70`, Actions run `29361336519`: focused suite passed (`src/commands/doctor-config-preflight.test.ts`, `src/commands/doctor-config-flow.test.ts`, `src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts`, `src/flows/doctor-core-checks.test.ts`, `src/commands/doctor-session-transcripts.test.ts`, `src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.test.ts`, `src/config/config.legacy-config-detection.accepts-imessage-dmpolicy.test.ts`, `extensions/imessage/src/doctor-contract-api.test.ts`): 4 shards, 253 passed, 2 skipped, exitCode 0.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox isolated doctor proof on the same lease and current head: `corepack pnpm dev doctor --fix --yes` against a temp config with both stale keys exited 0; post-run JSON check reported `hasTop=false`, `hasAccount=false`; stdout included both retired-key removal lines and `Doctor complete.` Lease was stopped after proof.\n- Local focused tests after the repair fix: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-config-preflight.test.ts src/commands/doctor-config-flow.test.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts src/flows/doctor-core-checks.test.ts src/commands/doctor-session-transcripts.test.ts src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.test.ts src/config/config.legacy-config-detection.accepts-imessage-dmpolicy.test.ts extensions/imessage/src/doctor-contract-api.test.ts` passed: 4 shards, 253 passed, 2 skipped.\n- Formatting/whitespace: `pnpm format:check -- src/commands/doctor-config-flow.ts src/commands/doctor-config-preflight.test.ts src/commands/doctor-config-preflight.ts src/commands/doctor-session-transcripts.ts src/flows/doctor-core-checks.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.ts src/flows/health-checks.ts src/config/validation.ts src/config/config.legacy-config-detection.accepts-imessage-dmpolicy.test.ts && git diff --check` passed.\n- Autoreview: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode commit --commit HEAD` passed clean after one accepted finding was fixed; no accepted/actionable findings remained, overall patch correct (0.86).\n- Read-only local macOS/imsg proof: host has `imsg 0.12.3`; `imsg status --json` reported `ok=true`; `imsg chats --limit 5 --json` returned 5 readable chats with only redacted metadata inspected. Version comparison probe accepted `0.12.3`, rejected `0.11.0`, and rejected `0.11.1-beta.1` against minimum `0.11.1`.\n- Live send/URL-preview proof was not performed because no approved recipient/chat id was provided for sending real iMessages. No production Messages data or account identifiers are included in this PR body.\n",
        "branch": "agent/remove-imessage-split-send-coalescing-91243",
